  "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<9,\\,-1<y<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{xy}},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<9,\\,1<y<4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(1,9)\\times (-1,1)$ and ${R}_{2}=(1,9)\\times (1,4).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =(9-1){\\int }_{-1}^{1}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+({\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =8[{y}^{3}]_{-1}^{1}+[\\sqrt{x}]_{1}^{9}\\cdot [\\sqrt{y}]_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =8({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3})+(3-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
